-- SHADOW-SEMANTICS cell I15 (S1 scope, ruling #1375): the interface's home module IS
-- imported here -- and the interface still is not nameable, because the import binds only
-- `sf`. §1.0's `nameable in M` is about the DECLARATION a module may refer to by name, not
-- about which modules it touches, and this module cannot refer to `Sizeable` at all:
-- writing `impl Sizeable Blob` here is rejected `Unknown interface: Sizeable` (resolve,
-- `UnknownInterface`) -- on the base binary as well as this one, so it is not a property
-- this change created. So `size` is not a shadow here and the occurrence is the standalone
-- explicitly imported from `fmod`: 99.
--
-- WHY THIS CELL EXISTS: i12 pins the TRANSITIVE form of the same defect -- the interface's
-- module reached only through a third module that re-exports nothing. This is the ONE-HOP
-- form, and it is one line SHORTER: #1353's own repro with the bridge removed. The first
-- cut of that fix admitted a dependency's WHOLE interface set on any import of it, so this
-- shape still printed 7 while i12 was green -- the S0 narrowed rather than fixed, with its
-- must-fail pin already deleted. A one-hop cell and a transitive cell are NOT the same
-- test; the transitive one passes while the one-hop one is broken.
import fmod.{size}
import smod.{sf}

main = println (size "abc" + sf 0)
